  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Myla Babji And Another vs The State Of Andhra Pradesh on 21 July, 2020 Author: J.K. Maheshwari Bench: J.K. Maheshwari High Court Of Andhra Pradesh: Amaravati Chief Justice J.K. Maheshwari Criminal Petition No.2601 of 2020 Myla Babji and another ...",
    "facts": "",
    "arguments": "Counsel for the petitioners has placed reliance on the common order dated 18.12.2019 passed by a coordinate Bench of this Court in Criminal Petition Nos.5421 of 2019 and batch, holding that \"tobacco\" does not fall within the definition of \"food\", as specified under Section 3(i)(j) of the Act, therefore, registration of crime is not permissible . On the other hand, though the Public Prosecutor opposed the relief prayed for, but, he is not in a position to dispute the fact that various petitions filed before this Court under Section 482 Cr.P.C. have been allowed and crimes have been [LEAKAGE_MASK] on the basis of the analogy has put forth by the petitioners before this Court. Myla Babji And Another vs The State Of Andhra Pradesh on 21 July, 2020 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/57889624/ 1",
    "petitioner_arguments": "Counsel for the petitioners has placed reliance on the common order dated 18.12.2019 passed by a coordinate Bench of this Court in Criminal Petition Nos.5421 of 2019 and batch, holding that \"tobacco\" does not fall within the definition of \"food\", as specified under Section 3(i)(j) of the Act, therefore, registration of crime is not permissible . On the other hand, though the Public Prosecutor opposed the relief prayed for, but, he is not in a position to dispute the fact that various petitions filed before this Court under Section 482 Cr.P.C. have been allowed and crimes have been [LEAKAGE_MASK] on the basis of the analogy has put forth by the petitioners before this Court. Myla Babji And Another vs The State Of Andhra Pradesh on 21 July, 2020 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/57889624/ 1",
